Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement. Question: How accurate must the fundamental representations and warranties be according to the bring down provision? Option A: Accurate at another materiality standard (e.g., hybrid standard) Option B: Accurate in all material respects Option C: Accurate in all respects. Merger Agreement: (b) Additional Conditions to Obligation of Buyer. The representations and warranties of the Company set forth in Article 4 shall be true and accurate as of the Closing Date, except for inaccuracies that do not have a material adverse effect on the Company. (Page 45) Merger Agreement: Section 9.1 Conditions to Closing. The representations and warranties made by the Company in this Agreement must be accurate in all respects as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing, except for minor inaccuracies that are not expected to individually or in the aggregate have a material adverse effect. (Page 112)
